  "history": "TCV was founded in 1995 by Jay Hoag and Rick Kimball, who closed its first fund that June. It backed Netflix, Facebook, Airbnb, Spotify and ByteDance as private companies and often held on after they listed, the crossover in its name. Its largest fund, TCV XI, closed at $4 billion in 2021; it manages $23 billion from Menlo Park, New York and London, and the track record on this page covers its minority stakes only.",
